@@ -326,7 +326,7 @@ short. View 5: the `cps.*` and `cpsf.*` keys moved from `storage` to `cps` (27),
 | # | Section | Keys |
 |---|---|---|
 | 0 | `core` | `view state tx_deny can_tx txlim txlim.n txlim.refused txlim.last_hz mode am bcast bcast_fault bcast_khz vfo vfo_index` (`am` 1: received in AM, the air band; `bcast` 1: heard on the broadcast receiver, `bcast_fault` 1 when it didn't answer, `bcast_khz` the frequency the receiver reports; [airband-and-broadcast.md](airband-and-broadcast.md)) (which VFO: 0, or 1 the second; `radio-features.md` 2.1) `zone_index zone_pos zone_size zone_count zone_name channel_number channel_name rx_hz tx_hz power power_name power_count power_names tx_drive pa_keyup pa_keyup.last bands temporary temp squelch monitor tone_ok rssi_dbm noise tx_elapsed_ms tot_s last_rx_ms last_tx_ms tx_auto wakes vfo_step_hz vfo_drop codeplug hotspot`, `vfo_drop` a saved VFO's mode (`radio_mode_t` + 1) that this build or board can't run, so the VFO came back at power-up in the default mode instead (0 none), `bands` the board's bands in Hz (`lo-hi`, comma separated), `last_tx_ms` when the last transmission began (0 none), `tx_auto` 1 when that transmission is the radio's own (a data list such as ARS, a roaming probe, an APRS beacon), `wakes` 1 while the radio state lights the screen (`radio_view_wakes`, [ui.md](ui.md)), `rssi_dbm` is the raw reading in FM and idle, and the peak of the last `RADIO_RSSI_HOLD_MS` (120 ms, two TDMA frames) while the DMR stack runs; `call.rssi_dbm` is the modem's per-burst level, else the held one; `txlim` the test TX limit (op 35): `off`, `block` or `list`, with `txlim.n` frequencies; `txlim.refused` keyings it refused since the start, the last at `txlim.last_hz`; `power_names` every power level's name at the channel's transmit frequency, lowest first, `/` between (`board_power_name`: a radio whose top level differs by band names it per band); `tx_drive` (radios with `hal_radio_t.tx_drive_level`) the PA drive of each power level at the channel's transmit frequency, lowest first, `/` between (0: the level doesn't transmit there); `pa_keyup` (radios with the DMR PA key-up, [pa-keyup.md](pa-keyup.md)) its constants blend/top/hold % and boost/hold/PA µs before the first symbol (RADIO op 37), and `pa_keyup.last` the last key-up's boost/hold/drive (boost 0: none); `req_handled req_dropped` (radio requests taken by the radio task; lost to a full queue), `ch_read_errors` (reads of a used channel that failed: flash read or record decode), `serial` |
-| 1 | `channel` | `ch.name ch.rx_hz ch.tx_hz ch.mode ch.kind ch.bw ch.rx_tone ch.tx_tone ch.power ch.rx_only ch.color_code ch.timeslot ch.contact ch.listen_list ch.dmr_id ch.dmo ch.tone_burst ch.sfr` (`ch.sfr`: the stored SFR bytes A,B, `0,0` = none; `ch.kind`: the channel's kind, [channel-modes.md](channel-modes.md) 4, 0 a plain channel) |
