+
+Select a conventional FM channel or tune the FM VFO. Stop scan or dual watch and open **Tools > Tone search**.
+Choose **Search CTCSS** or **Search DCS**. The radio waits for a carrier and checks the standard tones or codes.
+Searching DCS covers both normal and inverted codes and may take up to about 95 seconds of carrier time.
+
+The detected tone appears beside **Use for RX**. Select it to use the result for receive squelch. On a memory
+channel use **Save channel** to keep it. **Back** leaves the current tone alone. The first press of PTT during
